      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: seagulls_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts three seagulls standing on rocks near water, with text that reads: 'fine, i'll keep calling them seagulls.. ...but, beach chickens sounds better.' The intent is to humorously suggest an alternative, more colloquial or playful name for seagulls ('beach chickens'), which is a lighthearted and non-offensive pun. There is no toxicity, hate, abuse, or harmful content present. The humor is based on wordplay and casual naming, not on disparaging any group or community. The term 'beach chickens' is not a derogatory stereotype and does not map onto any of the harmful categories listed in the knowledge base. The overall intent is to entertain through linguistic humor, not to cause harm or promote hate.",
