      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "beach_chickens",
      "label": "beach chickens",
      "description": "A colloquial, informal, and playful term used to refer to seagulls, especially in beach or coastal settings. It is not a derogatory or offensive term, but rather a humorous, lighthearted nickname that implies a more casual or 'down-to-earth' identity for the birds, contrasting with the more formal or scientific term 'seagull'. This term is part of a broader cultural trend of using whimsical or anthropomorphic nicknames for animals or common objects.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_681442e6"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a2fd00e4",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "seagull_naming_convention",
      "label": "seagull naming convention",
      "description": "The common practice of referring to the gull family of birds (genus Larus) as 'seagulls' in casual or colloquial contexts, despite the fact that not all gulls are coastal or marine birds. The term 'seagull' is widely accepted and used in everyday language, even though it is technically imprecise. The meme plays on this by suggesting a more playful alternative name.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_681442e6"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2774e6f5",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "bird_nickname_culture",
      "label": "bird nickname culture",
      "description": "A cultural phenomenon where people assign informal, often humorous or affectionate nicknames to birds or other animals based on their appearance, behavior, or habitat. This is common in social media, memes, and casual conversation, and often serves to humanize or anthropomorphize animals. The term 'beach chickens' fits into this category as a playful rebranding.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
